---@class twitch.ChatSettingsUpdated
---@field broadcaster_id string The ID of the broadcaster specified in the request.
---@field emote_mode boolean A Boolean value that determines whether chat messages must contain only emotes. Is **true** if chat messages may contain only emotes; otherwise, **false**.
---@field follower_mode boolean A Boolean value that determines whether the broadcaster restricts the chat room to followers only. Is **true** if the broadcaster restricts the chat room to followers only; otherwise, **false**. See the `follower_mode_duration` field for how long users must follow the broadcaster before being able to participate in the chat room.
---@field follower_mode_duration number|distilled.Null The length of time, in minutes, that users must follow the broadcaster before being able to participate in the chat room. Is **null** if `follower_mode` is **false**.
---@field moderator_id? string The moderator’s ID. The response includes this field only if the request specifies a user access token that includes the **moderator:read:chat\_settings** scope.
---@field non_moderator_chat_delay boolean A Boolean value that determines whether the broadcaster adds a short delay before chat messages appear in the chat room. This gives chat moderators and bots a chance to remove them before viewers can see the message. See the `non_moderator_chat_delay_duration` field for the length of the delay. Is **true** if the broadcaster applies a delay; otherwise, **false**.
---@field non_moderator_chat_delay_duration number|distilled.Null The amount of time, in seconds, that messages are delayed before appearing in chat. Is **null** if `non_moderator_chat_delay` is **false**.
---@field slow_mode boolean A Boolean value that determines whether the broadcaster limits how often users in the chat room are allowed to send messages. Is **true** if the broadcaster applies a delay; otherwise, **false**. See the `slow_mode_wait_time` field for the delay.
---@field slow_mode_wait_time number|distilled.Null The amount of time, in seconds, that users must wait between sending messages. Is **null** if slow\_mode is **false**.
---@field subscriber_mode boolean A Boolean value that determines whether only users that subscribe to the broadcaster’s channel may talk in the chat room. Is **true** if the broadcaster restricts the chat room to subscribers only; otherwise, **false**.
---@field unique_chat_mode boolean A Boolean value that determines whether the broadcaster requires users to post only unique messages in the chat room. Is **true** if the broadcaster requires unique messages only; otherwise, **false**.

