---@class twitch.SendChatAnnouncementRequest
---@field broadcaster_id string The ID of the broadcaster that owns the chat room to send the announcement to.
---@field moderator_id string The ID of a user who has permission to moderate the broadcaster’s chat room, or the broadcaster’s ID if they’re sending the announcement.
---@field message string The announcement to make in the broadcaster’s chat room. Announcements are limited to a maximum of 500 characters; announcements longer than 500 characters are truncated.
---@field color? twitch.SendChatAnnouncementRequestColor|string The color used to highlight the announcement. Possible case-sensitive values are: * blue * green * orange * purple * primary (default) If `color` is set to _primary_ or is not set, the channel’s accent color is used to highlight the announcement (see **Profile Accent Color** under [profile settings](https://www.twitch.tv/settings/profile), **Channel and Videos**, and **Brand**).
---@field for_source_only? boolean **NOTE:** This parameter can only be set when utilizing an App Access Token. It cannot be specified when a User Access Token is used, and will instead result in an HTTP 400 error. Determines if the chat announcement is sent only to the source channel (defined by _broadcaster\_id_) during a shared chat session. This has no effect if the announcement is not sent during a shared chat session. The default value when using an App Access Token is `true`. If you prefer to send an announcement to all channels in a shared chat session, set this parameter to `false`.

---The color used to highlight the announcement. Possible case-sensitive values are:
---
---* blue
---* green
---* orange
---* purple
---* primary (default)
---
---If `color` is set to _primary_ or is not set, the channel’s accent color is used to highlight the announcement (see **Profile Accent Color** under [profile settings](https://www.twitch.tv/settings/profile), **Channel and Videos**, and **Brand**).
---@alias twitch.SendChatAnnouncementRequestColor "blue"|"green"|"orange"|"purple"|"primary"

---@class twitch.SendChatAnnouncementResponse

---@class twitch.SendChatMessageRequest
---@field broadcaster_id string The ID of the broadcaster whose chat room the message will be sent to.
---@field sender_id string The ID of the user sending the message. This ID must match the user ID in the user access token.
---@field message string The message to send. The message is limited to a maximum of 500 characters. Chat messages can also include emoticons. To include emoticons, use the name of the emote. The names are case sensitive. Don’t include colons around the name (e.g., :bleedPurple:). If Twitch recognizes the name, Twitch converts the name to the emote before writing the chat message to the chat room
---@field reply_parent_message_id? string The ID of the chat message being replied to.
---@field for_source_only? boolean **NOTE:** This parameter can only be set when utilizing an App Access Token. It cannot be specified when a User Access Token is used, and will instead result in an HTTP 400 error. Determines if the chat message is sent only to the source channel (defined by _broadcaster\_id_) during a shared chat session. This has no effect if the message is not sent during a shared chat session. If this parameter is not set, the default value when using an App Access Token is `false`. On May 19, 2025 the default value for this parameter will be updated to `true`, and chat messages sent using an App Access Token will only be shared with the source channel by default. If you prefer to send a chat message to both channels in a shared chat session, make sure this parameter is explicitly set to `false` in your API request before May 19.
---@field pin? boolean NEW If true, the message will be sent and immediately pinned. Default: false. Cannot be combined with `reply_parent_message_id` or `for_source_only`. When `pin` is true, additionally requires the `moderator:manage:chat_messages` scope and the sender must be the broadcaster or a moderator. Messages pinned via this endpoint are always pinned for 20 minutes. If the pin fails, the message is not sent.

---@class twitch.SendChatMessageResponse
---@field data twitch.SendChatMessageResponseDataList

---@class twitch.SendChatMessageResponseDataItem
---@field message_id string The message id for the message that was sent.
---@field is_sent boolean If the message passed all checks and was sent.
---@field drop_reason? twitch.SendChatMessageResponseDataItemDropReason The reason the message was dropped, if any.

---The reason the message was dropped, if any.
---@class twitch.SendChatMessageResponseDataItemDropReason
---@field code string Code for why the message was dropped.
---@field message string Message for why the message was dropped.

---@alias twitch.SendChatMessageResponseDataList twitch.SendChatMessageResponseDataItem[]

